Subject: [DEBUG, test builds only] soc: qcom: stats: log the AOP's CXPC violators after a system suspend (SM8550)

Not for release builds.  scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh applies this only
with APPLY_DEEP_SLEEP_DEBUG_SWITCHES=1 and refuses a default build in a source
tree that carries it.  No board check: an SM8550 (both tablets).

One switch, N at every boot, that root writes at run time:

  /sys/module/qcom_stats/parameters/debug_cxpc_violators

and two read-only debugfs files, qcom_stats/cxpc_violators and
qcom_stats/ddr_votes.

qcom_stats counts the SoC's AOSS sleeps, CX collapses and DDR low-power
entries (aosd, cxsd, ddr) but cannot say what held them off, and the
application processor's own sleep set (sleep-test.sh rpmh) is one RPMh
requester (DRV) of about twenty.  The AOP keeps a log of the DRVs that
voted against CX power collapse while the APPS slept, when it is asked
with a QMP message before the suspend; Samsung's kernel for this SoC and
firmware reads it (drivers/soc/qcom/sys_pm_vx.c, compatible
"qcom,sys-pm-kalama": the message "{class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, dur: 1000,
flush: 10, ts_adj: 1}" from its suspend callback, the log at
sys-pm-vx@c320000, 0x400 bytes, in its DTB, a header and lines of a time
word and a byte per DRV, an all-zero line where CX collapsed; the DRV
names below are its drv_names_kalama[]).  The kit does not change the DTB,
which has no node for the log, so the region is the SoC's address and is
mapped on an SM8550 alone, with the AOSS QMP that qcom_stats already uses
for the DDR stats.

With Y each system suspend sends the message from a PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE
notifier (process context, before the freeze), and the PM_POST_SUSPEND
notifier logs the log, at info level:

  cxpc violators: the AOP's CXPC monitor is on for this suspend
  cxpc violators: mode 0xcc (CXPC), N of M lines, every 1000 ms, ...
  cxpc violators: TIME: AUDIO 3, HLOS 1      (a line with DRVs in it)
  cxpc violators: TIME: CXPC enter            (an all-zero line)
  cxpc violators: summary: N lines, K of them CXPC enter or exit; DRVs: AUDIO 30/30 (every line), ...

What a DRV's value means beyond "this requester voted against CXPC" is
the AOP's and is not documented: the values are logged as they are.
qcom_stats/cxpc_violators shows the log as the AOP last left it, any time.
qcom_stats/ddr_votes asks the AOP for every DRV's DDR vote now
("{class: ddr, res: drvs_ddr_votes}", as soc_sleep_stats.c's
ddr_stats_get_ss_vote_info() does for kalama's 20 DRVs: they follow the
DDR stats' entries in the stats region qcom_stats maps) and shows ab and
ib; it is the awake state, for a DDR held at a frequency that no Linux
vote explains (the 547 MHz with the audio DSP stopped, revisions 9 and
10), and the order of its DRVs is taken to be the log's.

Before the switch is written nothing of this runs: the notifier returns
at once, the region is mapped and not read, and the debugfs files read
nothing until they are read.  Refused before SYSTEM_RUNNING (-EPERM), so
the kernel command line cannot set it; -ENODEV without the region or the
QMP.  Reading the region is the first access to that part of the AOP's
message RAM on this port (Samsung's HLOS, under the same hypervisor, reads
it): sleep-test.sh reads the debugfs file once right before it freezes
anything, so that a bus error, if the region were not mapped for this VM,
would come there and not in a sleep.

Kit revision 13: the first read (kit revision 12, SM-X710, 2026-11-24, one
suspend-to-idle of 30 s) gave a header that is no CXPC log's: mode 0xdb
(Samsung's decoder knows 0xaa AOSS, 0xcc CXPC, 0xdd DDR), "every 16 ms",
time shift 50 and flush 1 for the message's cxpc, 1000 ms and 10; and 26
lines whose "DRVs" were byte 0 of each of their six words in every line
(TZ, SECPROC, GPU, TME_HW, WLAN BB, DDR AUX) with small values and zero
bytes around them: 32-bit words, not a byte per DRV.  The layout read is
Samsung's (sys_pm_vx.c read_vx_data(): the type and size in the first word,
duration, shift and flush in the second, then per line a time word and a
byte per DRV in words), so the content, not the decode, is other than
expected; what it is and whether the message changed it cannot be told
from the decoded lines (zero bytes are not printed, and a shift of 50 on a
32-bit word is undefined: the times printed are the low 14 bits shifted by
18).  So the lines are decoded only under a CXPC header (mode 0xcc, a time
shift below 32), and the region is logged raw, 16 kernel lines of 16 words
("cxpc violators: raw ..."), right before the message, right after the AOP
took it (when it differs) and after the suspend (when it differs); a header
that is not a CXPC log's gives "cxpc violators: summary: not a CXPC log
(mode ...)".  qcom_stats/cxpc_violators_raw (0400) shows the region raw at
any time; sleep-test.sh cxpc reads it before it freezes anything.  Each
word is read with readl_relaxed() (the message RAM takes 32-bit reads).

---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_stats.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_stats.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
 #include <linux/seq_file.h>
+#include <linux/suspend.h>
 
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.h>
 #include <linux/soc/qcom/smem.h>
@@ -300,6 +301,454 @@ static void qcom_create_subsystem_stat_f
 				    &qcom_subsystem_sleep_stats_fops);
 }
 
+/*
+ * SM8550 deep-sleep debug, not for release builds: the AOP's log of what
+ * keeps the SoC out of CX power collapse, which
+ * scripts/build-mainline-kernel.sh adds only with
+ * APPLY_DEEP_SLEEP_DEBUG_SWITCHES=1 (qcom-stats-cxpc-violators-diagnostic.patch).
+ *
+ * qcom_stats counts the SoC's sleeps (aosd, cxsd, ddr) but cannot say what
+ * held them off.  The AOP can: asked with a QMP message, it keeps a log in
+ * its message RAM of each RPMh DRV (requester) that voted against CX power
+ * collapse while the application processor slept, a line every so often
+ * with a byte per DRV, an all-zero line when CX did collapse.  Samsung's
+ * kernel reads it on the same SoC and firmware (drivers/soc/qcom/
+ * sys_pm_vx.c, "qcom,sys-pm-kalama": the message
+ * "{class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, dur: 1000, flush: 10, ts_adj: 1}" before a
+ * suspend, the log at sys-pm-vx@c320000, 0x400 bytes, in its DTB, read
+ * after it, with the kalama DRV names below).  This kernel's DTB has no node
+ * for it and the kit does not change the DTB, so the region is the SoC's
+ * address, for an SM8550 alone.
+ *
+ * One switch, which root writes at run time and nothing else changes:
+ * /sys/module/qcom_stats/parameters/debug_cxpc_violators, N at every boot,
+ * refused before SYSTEM_RUNNING (the kernel command line cannot set it),
+ * -ENODEV off an SM8550 or without the AOSS QMP.  With Y each system
+ * suspend sends the message from its PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE notifier, and its
+ * PM_POST_SUSPEND notifier logs the log: "qcom_stats: cxpc violators:" lines,
+ * the header, then each line with a DRV in it by name and value, the CXPC
+ * lines ("CXPC enter" or "CXPC exit"), and a summary of which DRVs were in
+ * every line.  What a DRV's value means beyond "this requester held CX" is
+ * the AOP's and not documented; the values are logged as they are.  The
+ * read-only debugfs file qcom_stats/cxpc_violators (0400) shows the log as
+ * the AOP last left it, any time, and qcom_stats/ddr_votes (0400) asks the
+ * AOP for each DRV's DDR vote now ("{class: ddr, res: drvs_ddr_votes}",
+ * soc_sleep_stats.c's ddr_stats_get_ss_vote_info(), 20 DRVs on kalama,
+ * after the DDR stats' entries) and shows them, ab and ib, by the same
+ * names (the AOP's order of that list is taken to be the log's).  Nothing
+ * of this runs or reads until the switch is written or a file is read.
+ *
+ * Kit revision 12's first run read a region whose header is not a CXPC
+ * log's (mode 0xdb, "every 16 ms", time shift 50, flush 1, for the message's
+ * cxpc, 1000 ms and 10) and whose lines are 32-bit words, not a byte per
+ * DRV.  So the lines are decoded only under a CXPC header (mode 0xcc, a
+ * time shift below 32), and the region is logged raw, 0x400 bytes as 16
+ * lines of 16 words each, "cxpc violators: raw ..." in the kernel log: as
+ * it was right before the message, right after the AOP took it (when it
+ * differs) and after the suspend (when it differs), so that one run tells
+ * what the AOP writes there and when.  The read-only debugfs file
+ * qcom_stats/cxpc_violators_raw (0400) shows the region raw the same way.
+ * The message RAM takes 32-bit reads alone: each word is read with
+ * readl_relaxed().
+ */
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_BASE_SM8550	0x0c320000
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_SIZE		0x400
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_CXPC		0xcc
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_MAX_LINES		64
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS		(QCOM_STATS_VX_SIZE / 4)
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_ROW		16
+#define QCOM_STATS_DDR_VOTE_DRVS	20
+#define QCOM_STATS_DRV_ABSENT		0xdeaddead
+#define QCOM_STATS_DRV_INVALID		0xffffdead
+
+static const char * const qcom_stats_vx_drvs[] = {
+	"TZ", "HYP", "HLOS", "L3", "SECPROC", "AUDIO", "AOP", "DEBUG",
+	"GPU", "DISPLAY", "COMPUTE_DSP", "TME_SW", "TME_HW", "MDM SW",
+	"MDM HW", "WLAN RF", "WLAN BB", "CAM_IFE0", "CAM_IFE1", "CAM_IFE2",
+	"DDR AUX", "ARC CPRF",
+};
+
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV	ARRAY_SIZE(qcom_stats_vx_drvs)
+/* A line: its time word, then a byte per DRV in words. */
+#define QCOM_STATS_VX_LINE	(4 + 4 * DIV_ROUND_UP(QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV, 4))
+
+static void __iomem *qcom_stats_vx_base;
+static void __iomem *qcom_stats_ddr_base;
+static bool qcom_stats_vx_on;
+static bool qcom_stats_vx_armed;
+/* The region right before the message and right after the AOP took it. */
+static u32 qcom_stats_vx_snap[2][QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS];
+static bool qcom_stats_vx_snapped[2];
+
+struct qcom_stats_vx_log {
+	u8 type, logsize, ts_shift, flush;
+	u16 dur_ms;
+	unsigned int lines;
+	u32 ts[QCOM_STATS_VX_MAX_LINES];
+	u8 drv[QCOM_STATS_VX_MAX_LINES][QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV];
+};
+
+static int qcom_stats_vx_read(struct qcom_stats_vx_log *log)
+{
+	unsigned int max, i, j;
+	u32 w0, w1, v = 0;
+	void __iomem *p;
+
+	w0 = readl_relaxed(qcom_stats_vx_base);
+	w1 = readl_relaxed(qcom_stats_vx_base + 4);
+	if (!w0 || !w1)
+		return -ENOENT;
+
+	log->type = w0 & 0xff;
+	log->logsize = (w0 >> 8) & 0xff;
+	log->dur_ms = w1 & 0xffff;
+	log->ts_shift = (w1 >> 16) & 0xff;
+	log->flush = w1 >> 24;
+	log->lines = 0;
+	/* Not the answer to the message: the lines are not decoded. */
+	if (log->type != QCOM_STATS_VX_CXPC || log->ts_shift >= 32)
+		return -EPROTO;
+
+	max = min3((unsigned int)log->logsize, (unsigned int)QCOM_STATS_VX_MAX_LINES,
+		   (unsigned int)((QCOM_STATS_VX_SIZE - 8) / QCOM_STATS_VX_LINE));
+	for (i = 0; i < max; i++) {
+		p = qcom_stats_vx_base + 8 + i * QCOM_STATS_VX_LINE;
+		log->ts[i] = readl_relaxed(p);
+		if (!log->ts[i])
+			break;
+		for (j = 0; j < QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV; j++) {
+			if (!(j % 4))
+				v = readl_relaxed(p + 4 + j);
+			log->drv[i][j] = (v >> (8 * (j % 4))) & 0xff;
+		}
+	}
+	log->lines = i;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static void qcom_stats_vx_copy(u32 *w)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS; i++)
+		w[i] = readl_relaxed(qcom_stats_vx_base + 4 * i);
+}
+
+/* The region raw, 16 kernel lines of 16 words, with when it was read. */
+static void qcom_stats_vx_dump(const char *when, const u32 *w)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS; i += QCOM_STATS_VX_ROW)
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: raw %s +0x%03x: %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x %08x\n",
+			when, 4 * i, w[i], w[i + 1], w[i + 2], w[i + 3], w[i + 4], w[i + 5], w[i + 6],
+			w[i + 7], w[i + 8], w[i + 9], w[i + 10], w[i + 11], w[i + 12], w[i + 13],
+			w[i + 14], w[i + 15]);
+}
+
+static bool qcom_stats_vx_line_empty(const struct qcom_stats_vx_log *log, unsigned int i)
+{
+	unsigned int j;
+
+	for (j = 0; j < QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV; j++)
+		if (log->drv[i][j])
+			return false;
+	return true;
+}
+
+/* One line of the log as text: the DRVs in it, or CXPC entered/left. */
+static void qcom_stats_vx_line(const struct qcom_stats_vx_log *log, unsigned int i,
+			       bool *in_cxpc, char *buf, size_t len)
+{
+	unsigned int j;
+	size_t n = 0;
+
+	if (qcom_stats_vx_line_empty(log, i)) {
+		scnprintf(buf, len, "CXPC %s", *in_cxpc ? "exit" : "enter");
+		*in_cxpc = !*in_cxpc;
+		return;
+	}
+	buf[0] = '\0';
+	for (j = 0; j < QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV; j++)
+		if (log->drv[i][j])
+			n += scnprintf(buf + n, len - n, "%s%s %u", n ? ", " : "",
+				       qcom_stats_vx_drvs[j], log->drv[i][j]);
+}
+
+static void qcom_stats_vx_report(void)
+{
+	struct qcom_stats_vx_log *log;
+	unsigned int i, j, held, some;
+	bool in_cxpc = false;
+	char *buf, *all;
+	size_t na = 0;
+	u32 *now;
+	int ret;
+
+	log = kzalloc(sizeof(*log), GFP_KERNEL);
+	buf = kzalloc(256, GFP_KERNEL);
+	all = kzalloc(256, GFP_KERNEL);
+	now = kcalloc(QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS, sizeof(*now), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!log || !buf || !all || !now)
+		goto out;
+
+	/*
+	 * The region raw: before the message, after it and now, each one
+	 * that differs from the one before it in full.
+	 */
+	qcom_stats_vx_copy(now);
+	if (qcom_stats_vx_snapped[0])
+		qcom_stats_vx_dump("before the message", qcom_stats_vx_snap[0]);
+	if (qcom_stats_vx_snapped[1]) {
+		if (qcom_stats_vx_snapped[0] &&
+		    !memcmp(qcom_stats_vx_snap[1], qcom_stats_vx_snap[0], QCOM_STATS_VX_SIZE))
+			pr_info("cxpc violators: raw after the message: the same as before it\n");
+		else
+			qcom_stats_vx_dump("after the message", qcom_stats_vx_snap[1]);
+	}
+	if (qcom_stats_vx_snapped[1] && !memcmp(now, qcom_stats_vx_snap[1], QCOM_STATS_VX_SIZE))
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: raw after the suspend: the same as after the message\n");
+	else
+		qcom_stats_vx_dump("after the suspend", now);
+
+	ret = qcom_stats_vx_read(log);
+	if (ret == -EPROTO) {
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: mode %#x, %u lines at most, every %u ms, time shift %u, flush %u: not a CXPC log (mode 0xcc, a time shift below 32), not decoded\n",
+			log->type, log->logsize, log->dur_ms, log->ts_shift, log->flush);
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: summary: not a CXPC log (mode %#x); the region raw is above\n",
+			log->type);
+		goto out;
+	}
+	if (ret) {
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: no log in the AOP's message RAM after this suspend\n");
+		goto out;
+	}
+	pr_info("cxpc violators: mode %#x%s, %u of %u lines, every %u ms, time shift %u, flush %u\n",
+		log->type, log->type == QCOM_STATS_VX_CXPC ? " (CXPC)" : "", log->lines,
+		log->logsize, log->dur_ms, log->ts_shift, log->flush);
+	for (i = 0; i < log->lines; i++) {
+		qcom_stats_vx_line(log, i, &in_cxpc, buf, 256);
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: %#x: %s\n", log->ts[i] << log->ts_shift, buf);
+	}
+	/* Which DRVs were in every line with a DRV in it, and which in some. */
+	for (j = 0, some = 0; j < QCOM_STATS_VX_NDRV; j++) {
+		for (i = 0, held = 0; i < log->lines; i++)
+			held += !!log->drv[i][j];
+		if (!held)
+			continue;
+		some++;
+		for (i = 0; i < log->lines; i++)
+			if (!log->drv[i][j] && !qcom_stats_vx_line_empty(log, i))
+				break;
+		na += scnprintf(all + na, 256 - na, "%s%s %u/%u%s", na ? ", " : "",
+				qcom_stats_vx_drvs[j], held, log->lines,
+				i == log->lines ? " (every line)" : "");
+	}
+	for (i = 0, held = 0; i < log->lines; i++)
+		held += qcom_stats_vx_line_empty(log, i);
+	pr_info("cxpc violators: summary: %u lines, %u of them CXPC enter or exit; DRVs: %s\n",
+		log->lines, held, some ? all : "none");
+out:
+	kfree(now);
+	kfree(all);
+	kfree(buf);
+	kfree(log);
+}
+
+static int qcom_stats_vx_pm_notify(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long action, void *data)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	switch (action) {
+	case PM_SUSPEND_PREPARE:
+		qcom_stats_vx_armed = false;
+		qcom_stats_vx_snapped[0] = qcom_stats_vx_snapped[1] = false;
+		if (!READ_ONCE(qcom_stats_vx_on))
+			break;
+		qcom_stats_vx_copy(qcom_stats_vx_snap[0]);
+		qcom_stats_vx_snapped[0] = true;
+		ret = qmp_send(qcom_stats_qmp, "{class: lpm_mon, type: cxpc, dur: 1000, flush: 10, ts_adj: 1}");
+		if (ret) {
+			pr_warn("cxpc violators: the AOP did not take the monitor message: %d\n", ret);
+			break;
+		}
+		qcom_stats_vx_copy(qcom_stats_vx_snap[1]);
+		qcom_stats_vx_snapped[1] = true;
+		qcom_stats_vx_armed = true;
+		pr_info("cxpc violators: the AOP's CXPC monitor is on for this suspend\n");
+		break;
+	case PM_POST_SUSPEND:
+		if (qcom_stats_vx_armed)
+			qcom_stats_vx_report();
+		qcom_stats_vx_armed = false;
+		break;
+	}
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
+static struct notifier_block qcom_stats_vx_nb = {
+	.notifier_call = qcom_stats_vx_pm_notify,
+};
+
+static int qcom_stats_vx_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	bool on;
+	int ret;
+
+	/* Run time only: see above. */
+	if (system_state != SYSTEM_RUNNING)
+		return -EPERM;
+
+	ret = kstrtobool(val, &on);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	if (on && (!qcom_stats_vx_base || !qcom_stats_qmp))
+		return -ENODEV;
+
+	WRITE_ONCE(*(bool *)kp->arg, on);
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct kernel_param_ops qcom_stats_vx_ops = {
+	.set = qcom_stats_vx_set,
+	.get = param_get_bool,
+};
+
+module_param_cb(debug_cxpc_violators, &qcom_stats_vx_ops, &qcom_stats_vx_on, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug_cxpc_violators,
+		 "debug: Y: log the AOP's CXPC violators after each system suspend (SM8550, run time only)");
+
+static int qcom_stats_vx_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
+{
+	struct qcom_stats_vx_log *log;
+	bool in_cxpc = false;
+	unsigned int i;
+	char *buf;
+	int ret;
+
+	log = kzalloc(sizeof(*log), GFP_KERNEL);
+	buf = kzalloc(256, GFP_KERNEL);
+	ret = -ENOMEM;
+	if (!log || !buf)
+		goto out;
+
+	ret = qcom_stats_vx_read(log);
+	if (ret == -EPROTO) {
+		seq_printf(s, "Mode: %#x, not a CXPC log (mode 0xcc, a time shift below 32): not decoded (cxpc_violators_raw has the region)\nDuration (ms): %u\nTime Shift: %u\nFlush Threshold: %u\nMax Log Entries: %u\n",
+			   log->type, log->dur_ms, log->ts_shift, log->flush, log->logsize);
+		ret = 0;
+		goto out;
+	}
+	if (ret) {
+		seq_puts(s, "no log\n");
+		ret = 0;
+		goto out;
+	}
+	seq_printf(s, "Mode: %#x%s\nDuration (ms): %u\nTime Shift: %u\nFlush Threshold: %u\nMax Log Entries: %u\n",
+		   log->type, log->type == QCOM_STATS_VX_CXPC ? " (CXPC)" : "", log->dur_ms,
+		   log->ts_shift, log->flush, log->logsize);
+	for (i = 0; i < log->lines; i++) {
+		qcom_stats_vx_line(log, i, &in_cxpc, buf, 256);
+		seq_printf(s, "%#x: %s\n", log->ts[i] << log->ts_shift, buf);
+	}
+	ret = 0;
+out:
+	kfree(buf);
+	kfree(log);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+DEFINE_SHOW_ATTRIBUTE(qcom_stats_vx);
+
+/* The region raw, as the kernel log has it: 16 lines of 16 words. */
+static int qcom_stats_vx_raw_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
+{
+	unsigned int i, j;
+	u32 *w;
+
+	w = kcalloc(QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS, sizeof(*w), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!w)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	qcom_stats_vx_copy(w);
+	for (i = 0; i < QCOM_STATS_VX_WORDS; i += QCOM_STATS_VX_ROW) {
+		seq_printf(s, "+0x%03x:", 4 * i);
+		for (j = 0; j < QCOM_STATS_VX_ROW; j++)
+			seq_printf(s, " %08x", w[i + j]);
+		seq_putc(s, '\n');
+	}
+	kfree(w);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
+DEFINE_SHOW_ATTRIBUTE(qcom_stats_vx_raw);
+
+static int qcom_stats_ddr_votes_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
+{
+	void __iomem *reg;
+	unsigned int i;
+	u32 n, v;
+	int ret;
+
+	/* After the magic, the entry count and the DDR stats' entries. */
+	n = readl_relaxed(qcom_stats_ddr_base + DDR_STATS_NUM_MODES_ADDR);
+	if (n > DDR_STATS_MAX_NUM_MODES)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	ret = qmp_send(qcom_stats_qmp, "{class: ddr, res: drvs_ddr_votes}");
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	reg = qcom_stats_ddr_base + DDR_STATS_ENTRY_START_ADDR + n * sizeof(struct ddr_stats_entry);
+	for (i = 0; i < QCOM_STATS_DDR_VOTE_DRVS; i++) {
+		v = readl_relaxed(reg + 4 * i);
+		seq_printf(s, "%-11s ", qcom_stats_vx_drvs[i]);
+		if (v == QCOM_STATS_DRV_ABSENT)
+			seq_puts(s, "absent\n");
+		else if (v == QCOM_STATS_DRV_INVALID)
+			seq_puts(s, "invalid\n");
+		else
+			seq_printf(s, "ab %u ib %u\n", (v >> 14) & 0x3fff, v & 0x3fff);
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
